name: substrate
include: .
-- ⟡agda-lib-stdlib: `depend: standard-library-2.3` removed. The substrate imports ZERO
-- stdlib modules (verified: 0 of ~1600 modules open Data./Relation./Function./Level./…;
-- the few `Agda.*` imports are the COMPILER's builtins, not the library). It reimplements
-- everything it needs. The declared dep only made `agda -i .` fail on any machine without
-- standard-library-2.3 installed — a dependency on something unused.

-- ⟡guardedness-global: `--guardedness` for the WHOLE library, in ONE place.
-- Verified before adopting: (a) Agda 2.8.0 emits NO warning when the flag is
-- present but unused (a purely-inductive module compiles silently); (b) the
-- tree uses NO `--sized-types` anywhere, so there is no `--safe` conflict;
-- (c) a module whose own pragma is `{-# OPTIONS --safe --without-K #-}` picks
-- the flag up from here with no ConflictingPragmaOptions — so NO per-file edit
-- is needed (1831 files left untouched); (d) this covers make,
-- full_build_check.py AND ad-hoc `agda -i.` probes, which command-line flags in
-- the two build scripts would not.
-- ⚑ It also DISSOLVES the InfectiveImport siting problem: that error fires only
-- at a boundary between a guardedness module and a non-guardedness one, and
-- globally there is no such boundary. Retires ⟡policy-guardedness-siting.
flags: --guardedness
